{
  "id": "29503_seigou",
  "headword": "{整合|せいごう}",
  "reading": "せいごう",
  "romaji": "seigou",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "consistency; conformity; alignment",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "consistency; conformity; alignment",
      "explanation": "The state of two or more things being consistent and free of contradiction, or the act of making them agree. Common in technical, logical, and administrative contexts such as data, theories, and rules."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29503_seigou_ex1",
      "japanese": "データの{整合|せいごう}を{取|と}る。",
      "english": "to make the data consistent.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29503_seigou_ex2",
      "japanese": "{二|ふた}つの{制度|せいど}の{整合|せいごう}を{図|はか}る。",
      "english": "to bring the two systems into alignment.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29503_seigou_ex3",
      "japanese": "{新|あたら}しい{規則|きそく}が{既存|きそん}の{法律|ほうりつ}と{整合|せいごう}するか{確認|かくにん}する{必要|ひつよう}がある。",
      "english": "We need to check whether the new rule is consistent with existing laws.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Combines {整|せい} (arrange, order) + {合|ごう} (match, fit). The condition of things fitting together without contradiction, or the act of making them do so. Frequent in technical and administrative writing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {整合|せいごう}を{取|と}る: to make things consistent\n- {整合|せいごう}{性|せい}: consistency (as a property)\n- {整合|せいごう}を{図|はか}る: to seek alignment\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {一致|いっち}: agreement; match — emphasizes things being identical or in accord\n- {矛盾|むじゅん}: contradiction — the opposite state, where things conflict",
